# The build context is copied wholesale by `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile.
# Anything listed here is either rebuilt inside the image, secret, or actively
# harmful to carry in.

# Rebuilt by `npm ci` in the deps stage.
node_modules

# The killer: a local .next left behind by `next dev` (webpack or turbopack)
# lands in the image and `next build` then runs on top of a manifest that
# describes a different router. That is what surfaces as
# "Cannot find module for page: /_document" during page data collection.
.next
out
build

# Local state that must never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
database.db
database.db-*
media

# Housekeeping
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
